      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds okay, but \"suggestive of efficacy\" might still make the investors nervous. they're going to ask if the results were actually significant. if i just say \"strong positive trends,\" they might dig into the math and see it missed the 0.05 mark. can we make the wording a bit more definitive? like, can we say the data shows clear evidence of the supplement working? i don't want to lie, but i also can't let this project die just because of a tiny margin.",
