      "content": "You should avoid definitive statements like \"clear evidence\" when the data doesn't meet the conventional $\\alpha=0.05$ threshold, as this could lead to major credibility issues. Instead, focus on the strength of the effect size you observed. Frame it by stating the observed effect size is substantial and warrants replication in a larger, powered study. This positions the $p$-value as a matter of sample size, not outcome, which sounds scientifically rigorous to investors.",
